# Generated by matugen from a wallpaper — qutebrowser browser-UI colors.
# Template: ~/.config/matugen/templates/qutebrowser-colors.py
# Do not edit this file by hand; edit the template and re-run matugen.
#
# Mapping rules — keep these when editing:
#   * dark surface (surface_container_lowest / _high) -> on_surface text
#   * primary / tertiary / error surface             -> the matching on_* text
#   * never set a .bg without its .fg: an unset .fg falls back to the Qt
#     palette, which on this machine comes from the GTK theme.
#   * the statusbar is ALWAYS dark. percentage / tabindex / backforward draw
#     themselves with QPainter using the widget palette
#     (mainwindow/statusbar/textbase.py), so colors.statusbar.*.fg does NOT
#     reach them — a bright statusbar background renders them unreadable.
#
# Website-side settings stay manual in colors.py:
#   colors.webpage.darkmode.*, colors.webpage.bg, c.hints.border.

# --- statusbar (dark on purpose, see note above) ---
